<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Models Used</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our experiments primarily utilized three open-source Large Language Models (LLMs): Mistral-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, Llama-3.2-8B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Grattafiori et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and Qwen2.5-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. For experiments involving closed-source models (as detailed in Table <a href="#S5.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 5.1 Overall Performance ‣ 5 Results and Analysis ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), we employed.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Unless otherwise specified, the same backbone LLM (from either the open-source or closed-source set, depending on the experiment) was consistently used for all stages of the CARE-RAG pipeline: eliciting the initial LLM response (<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\text{init}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>init</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\text{init}}</annotation></semantics></math>, corresponding to <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> generation in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), refining retrieved results into <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> (which may involve structured reasoning), conflict detection by <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> to produce <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, CARE-RAG to generate <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}</annotation></semantics></math>, and also for the QA Repair module (<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{repair}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>repair</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{repair}}</annotation></semantics></math>) described in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B QA Repair Module ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Retrieval Setup</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each question, we retrieved the top-K relevant evidences from the respective corpus. In our main experiments (Tables <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4.1 Datasets ‣ 4 Experimental Setup ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and <a href="#S5.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 5.1 Overall Performance ‣ 5 Results and Analysis ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), K was set to 5. An analysis of CARE-RAG’s sensitivity to varying K (from 5 to 25) is presented in Figure <a href="#S5.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 5.3 Sensitivity to Retrieval Volume ‣ 5 Results and Analysis ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Inference Framework</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All inferences for open-source LLMs were performed using the vLLM framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwon et al., 2023</a>)</cite> to ensure efficiency and reproducibility. For closed-source models, inferences were made via their respective official APIs.
The following inference parameters were consistently applied for generation tasks (e.g., generating initial responses for <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, the refined evidence <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, the final answer <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}</annotation></semantics></math>, and repaired answers in <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{repair}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>repair</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{repair}}</annotation></semantics></math>) unless a specific module (like the conflict detector <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>) required different settings:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">max_tokens</span>: 1024</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">temperature</span>: 0.7</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">top_p</span>: 1.0</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For classification-like tasks performed by the conflict detector <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> to determine <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> (and generate <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>), we typically used a temperature (e.g., 0.7, or potentially lower like 0.0 for more deterministic conflict/no-conflict output if desired) to encourage more deterministic outputs, though the primary mechanism for binary classification was specific instruction prompting tailored to elicit a "0" or "1" and a rationale.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Evaluation Metrics</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">System performance was primarily evaluated using standard Exact Match (EM) and F1 scores. These metrics were computed against the (potentially) repaired ground truth answers generated by our QA Repair module (detailed in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B QA Repair Module ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>), ensuring a fair and robust assessment across all compared methods.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>QA Repair Module</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Overview</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As highlighted in our experimental setup (Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Experimental Setup ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), standard QA benchmarks often suffer from issues such as temporal drift (outdated answers) or semantic mismatches between questions and ground truths. These flaws can lead to misleading evaluations of RAG systems. To ensure a fairer and more accurate assessment of model capabilities, we introduce a QA Repair module. This module is applied as a pre-processing step to the test instances of all evaluated benchmarks, correcting potential issues in the original ground truth answers before any model evaluation takes place. The module operates on an input triplet: (<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">question <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math></span>, <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">original ground truth answer</span> <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\text{gt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\text{gt}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and potentially relevant <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">retrieved context <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math></span>, though <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is not always strictly necessary for the repair logic if general world knowledge suffices).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Repair Mechanism</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The core of the QA Repair module is a classifier, <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{repair}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>repair</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{repair}}</annotation></semantics></math>, implemented using a prompted Large Language Model (LLM). This classifier is tasked with assessing whether the original ground truth answer, <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\text{gt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\text{gt}}</annotation></semantics></math>, is likely outdated, semantically inconsistent with the question <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, or otherwise flawed, considering current world knowledge and the precise intent of <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>. It outputs a binary flag:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\text{repair}}=f_{\text{repair}}(q,a_{\text{gt}},C_{\text{optional}})\in\{0,1\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mtext>repair</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>repair</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>optional</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\text{repair}}=f_{\text{repair}}(q,a_{\text{gt}},C_{\text{optional}})\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\text{repair}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mtext>repair</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\text{repair}}=1</annotation></semantics></math> (indicating a detected flaw), a repair process is initiated. This process, also typically leveraging a prompted LLM, employs structured reasoning or direct knowledge querying (based on <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> and potentially <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>) to generate a revised, more accurate ground truth answer, <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\prime}_{\text{gt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mtext>gt</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\prime}_{\text{gt}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In some instances, to resolve ambiguity or align with the corrected answer, the original question <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> might also be minimally refined to <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. The output of this stage is thus a potentially corrected question-answer pair <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q^{\prime},a^{\prime}_{\text{gt}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mtext>gt</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q^{\prime},a^{\prime}_{\text{gt}})</annotation></semantics></math>. This repaired pair is then used as the reference for evaluating all RAG models (including baselines and CARE-RAG) in our experiments.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Illustrative Examples</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following examples illustrate typical scenarios handled by the QA Repair module. Note that in these examples, "Current Model Answer" (if such a term was used previously, otherwise this clarification might not be needed) is re-interpreted as the "Repaired Ground Truth (<math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\prime}_{\text{gt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mtext>gt</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\prime}_{\text{gt}}</annotation></semantics></math>)" produced by our QA Repair module if a flaw was detected in the original "Ground Truth (<math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\text{gt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\text{gt}}</annotation></semantics></math>)".</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.3.1 </span>Example 1: Temporal Drift</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="286.37" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 286.37" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,286.37) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 281.53 C 0 284.2 2.17 286.37 4.84 286.37 L 648.31 286.37 C 650.98 286.37 653.15 284.2 653.15 281.53 L 653.15 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 0.69 L 0.69 281.53 C 0.69 283.82 2.55 285.68 4.84 285.68 L 648.31 285.68 C 650.6 285.68 652.46 283.82 652.46 281.53 L 652.46 0.69 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 139.11)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.26em;--ltx-fo-height:9.74em;--ltx-fo-depth:9.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="261.37" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 134.76)" width="612.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.26em;">
<span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Scenario: Temporal Drift</span><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.pic1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Original Query (<math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.pic1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Who scored the most points in their NBA career?</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.pic1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.pic1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Original Ground Truth (<math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\text{gt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#000000">gt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\text{gt}}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.pic1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Kareem Abdul-Jabbar</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.pic1.1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.pic1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">QA Repair Module Output<span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.pic1.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">:</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Detection (<math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\text{repair}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#000000">repair</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\text{repair}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: The answer "Kareem Abdul-Jabbar" is outdated.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Repaired Ground Truth (<math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\prime}_{\text{gt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#000000">gt</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\prime}_{\text{gt}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: </span><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">LeBron James</span><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (as of [current date/year of dataset repair])</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Repaired Query (<math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: (No change in this case) Who scored the most points in their NBA career?</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.3.2 </span>Example 2: Answer Type Mismatch / Factual Inaccuracy</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="303.74" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 303.74" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,303.74) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 298.9 C 0 301.58 2.17 303.74 4.84 303.74 L 648.31 303.74 C 650.98 303.74 653.15 301.58 653.15 298.9 L 653.15 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 0.69 L 0.69 298.9 C 0.69 301.19 2.55 303.05 4.84 303.05 L 648.31 303.05 C 650.6 303.05 652.46 301.19 652.46 298.9 L 652.46 0.69 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 155.72)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.26em;--ltx-fo-height:9.79em;--ltx-fo-depth:10.35em;font-size:10pt;" height="278.74" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 135.53)" width="612.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.26em;">
<span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Scenario: Answer Type Mismatch / Factual Inaccuracy</span><span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.pic1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Original Query (<math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.pic1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: When was the Statue of Liberty in France built?</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.pic1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.pic1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Original Ground Truth (<math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\text{gt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#000000">gt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\text{gt}}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.pic1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Paris</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.pic1.1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.pic1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">QA Repair Module Output<span id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.pic1.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">:</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Detection (<math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\text{repair}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#000000">repair</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\text{repair}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: The answer "Paris" does not answer "When" and is factually incorrect for the construction date.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Repaired Ground Truth (<math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\prime}_{\text{gt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#000000">gt</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\prime}_{\text{gt}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: </span><span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Construction was completed in July 1884.</span><span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (Or simply: </span><span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">July 1884</span><span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Repaired Query (<math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: (No change in this case) When was the Statue of Liberty in France built?</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.3.3 </span>Detailed Analysis of Repaired Data</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A2.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ B.3.3 Detailed Analysis of Repaired Data ‣ B.3 Illustrative Examples ‣ Appendix B QA Repair Module ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> details the error composition within corrected samples from five QA benchmarks (1,000 samples each were analyzed for repair needs). The chart displays the counts of "Mismatch" errors (semantic misalignment) and "Out-of-date" errors (temporal drift) among the instances that required repair. For example, all 67 repaired Wiki samples were out-of-date, while TriviaQA’s 74 repairs included approximately 33 mismatches. Notably, the NQ dataset, with 240 repaired samples, exhibits an overlap in error types: the sum of its reported mismatch (approx. 47) and out-of-date (approx. 196) components exceeds the total repair count, indicating some samples possess both error attributes. This granular analysis, highlighting diverse error profiles and potential co-occurrences as in NQ, underscores the necessity of our comprehensive QA Repair process for establishing a reliable evaluation baseline and the importance of targeted, rather than one-size-fits-all, approaches to dataset noise.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2507.01281v1/repair_error_visualization_hatch_final.png" id="A2.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/285;" width="429" height="285" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Mismatch and Out-of-date error distribution in repaired samples from five QA datasets. NQ shows co-occurring error types. Repair impact on Qwen2.5-7B (using the notation from your paper if Qwen3-235B-A22B is a specific variant) is detailed in Table <a href="#S3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 3 QA Repair for Valid Evaluation ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> (Please verify this table label and its content regarding repair impact specifically with this model version).</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Core Conflict-Aware and Reliable Evidence for RAG Prompts</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides the specific prompt formats used for the core stages of the Conflict-Aware and Reliable Evidence for RAG (CARE-RAG) framework, corresponding to the <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> symbols in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Parameter Record Comparison Prompts (<math id="A3.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\text{init}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>init</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\text{init}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\text{iter}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>iter</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\text{iter}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</h3>

<section id="A3.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.1.1 </span>Iterative parameter Response Prompt (<math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\text{iter}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>iter</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\text{iter}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Objective: Elicit alternative or more diverse parameter responses <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>), given the previously generated parameter responses within <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, to further explore the model’s internal knowledge space.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="171.34" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 171.34" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,171.34) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#808080;" fill="#808080" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 166.49 C 0 169.17 2.17 171.34 4.84 171.34 L 648.31 171.34 C 650.98 171.34 653.15 169.17 653.15 166.49 L 653.15 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 0.69 L 0.69 166.49 C 0.69 168.79 2.55 170.65 4.84 170.65 L 648.31 170.65 C 650.6 170.65 652.46 168.79 652.46 166.49 L 652.46 0.69 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.5 12.03)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:45.4em;--ltx-fo-height:10.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="154.21" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 150.75)" width="628.21"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:45.4em;">
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Task<span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Based on your previous answer(s) and your internal knowledge, provide a different or more detailed/nuanced answer to the following question.</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000B3;">Question</span><span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2.pic1.1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: {question}</span></span>
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2.pic1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2.pic1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC6600;">Previous parameter Answer(s) (<math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC6600;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#CC6600">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC6600;" mathcolor="#CC6600">p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> so far)</span><span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2.pic1.1.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: {previous_parameter_answers}</span></span>
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2.pic1.1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2.pic1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC6600;">Answer (Iterative - <math id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC6600;" mathcolor="#CC6600">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC6600;" mathcolor="#CC6600">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2.pic1.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:<span id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p2.pic1.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.1.2 </span>Initial parameter Response Prompt (<math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\text{init}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>init</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\text{init}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Objective: Elicit the model’s first direct response <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> based solely on its internal parameter knowledge, forming the basis of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="113.22" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 113.22" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,113.22) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#808080;" fill="#808080" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 108.38 C 0 111.05 2.17 113.22 4.84 113.22 L 648.31 113.22 C 650.98 113.22 653.15 111.05 653.15 108.38 L 653.15 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 0.69 L 0.69 108.38 C 0.69 110.67 2.55 112.53 4.84 112.53 L 648.31 112.53 C 650.6 112.53 652.46 110.67 652.46 108.38 L 652.46 0.69 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.5 12.03)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:45.4em;--ltx-fo-height:6.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="96.09" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 92.63)" width="628.21"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:45.4em;">
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Task<span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Provide a concise and direct answer to the following question using only your internal knowledge.</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000B3;">Question</span><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.pic1.1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: {question}</span></span>
<span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.pic1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.pic1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC6600;">Answer (Initial - <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC6600;" mathcolor="#CC6600">a</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC6600;" mathcolor="#CC6600">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.pic1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:<span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.pic1.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Retrieval Result Refinement Prompt (<math id="A3.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Objective: Instruct the model to distill the retrieved evidences <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> into a concise and salient context-aware evidence <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, by extracting key factual observations, identifying ambiguities, and forming context-grounded conclusions. This corresponds to Stage II in Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="400.68" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 400.68" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,400.68) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#B3B3B3;" fill="#B3B3B3" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 397.36 C 0 399.19 1.49 400.68 3.32 400.68 L 649.83 400.68 C 651.66 400.68 653.15 399.19 653.15 397.36 L 653.15 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.55 0.55 L 0.55 397.36 C 0.55 398.89 1.79 400.12 3.32 400.12 L 649.83 400.12 C 651.36 400.12 652.6 398.89 652.6 397.36 L 652.6 0.55 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.36 68.62)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:45.42em;--ltx-fo-height:23.39em;--ltx-fo-depth:4.35em;font-size:10pt;" height="383.83" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 323.64)" width="628.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:45.42em;">
<span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Context Refinement Prompt<span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000B3;">Instruction</span><span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:
Analyze the provided Context thoroughly in relation to the Question. Your goal is to extract the most relevant factual information, identify any ambiguities or limitations within the context, and conclude with the most likely answer(s) or key insights that can be *purely grounded in the provided Context*. If no complete answer is available from the context, state that and explain why.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC6600;">Retrieved Context evidences (<math id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC6600;" mathcolor="#CC6600">C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.8em;">
<span id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{context_evidence_1}</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{context_evidence_2}</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">…</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{context_evidence_k}</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#005959;">Question (<math id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#005959;" mathcolor="#005959">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span><span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
{question}</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;">Your Distilled Context-Aware evidence (<math id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#BF0040">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>) based *only* on the Retrieved Context should include</span><span id="A3.SS2.p2.pic1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span>
<span id="A3.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.8em;">
<span id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Key factual claims relevant to the Question.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Identified ambiguities or limitations in the provided Context.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">A concluding summary or answer candidate(s) strictly derived from the Context.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Conflict Detection Prompt (<math id="A3.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>)</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Objective: Explicitly evaluate whether the model’s consolidated parameter-aware evidences (<math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>) semantically conflict with the refined Context-aware evidence (<math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>). This is used by the conflict detector module <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and corresponds to Stage III in Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="287.57" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 287.57" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,287.57) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FF4040;" fill="#FF4040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 282.73 C 0 285.4 2.17 287.57 4.84 287.57 L 648.31 287.57 C 650.98 287.57 653.15 285.4 653.15 282.73 L 653.15 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 0.69 L 0.69 282.73 C 0.69 285.02 2.55 286.88 4.84 286.88 L 648.31 286.88 C 650.6 286.88 652.46 285.02 652.46 282.73 L 652.46 0.69 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.5 12.03)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:45.4em;--ltx-fo-height:19.29em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="270.44" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 266.98)" width="628.21"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:45.4em;">
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Conflict Detection Prompt<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000B3;">Instruction</span><span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Evaluate if the "parameter Knowledge Response" contradicts the "Context-derived Response" for the given Question. Consider factual differences (e.g., names, dates, values), temporal mismatches, or significant semantic inconsistencies.
Output ’Conflict: 1’ if a contradiction is found.
Output ’Conflict: 0’ if there is no contradiction or if they are consistent.
Provide a brief step-by-step reasoning for your decision.</span></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#005959;">Question (<math id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#005959;" mathcolor="#005959">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> {question}</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC6600;">parameter Knowledge Response (Consolidated from <math id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC6600;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#CC6600">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC6600;" mathcolor="#CC6600">p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> {consolidated_parameter_response}</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;">Context-derived Response (from <math id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#BF0040">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> {context_aware_evidence_summary}</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Analysis and Conflict Decision (<math id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c},r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c},r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>):<span id="A3.SS3.p2.pic1.1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>CARE-RAG Generation Prompt (<math id="A3.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\text{synth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>synth</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\text{synth}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Objective: Generate the final answer (<math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}</annotation></semantics></math>) by integrating the parameter-aware evidences (<math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>), the refined Context-aware evidence (<math id="A3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>), and the conflict detection signal (<math id="A3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c},r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c},r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>). This corresponds to Stage IV in Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="752.52" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 752.52" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,752.52) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#B3B3B3;" fill="#B3B3B3" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 749.2 C 0 751.04 1.49 752.52 3.32 752.52 L 649.83 752.52 C 651.66 752.52 653.15 751.04 653.15 749.2 L 653.15 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.55 0.55 L 0.55 749.2 C 0.55 750.73 1.79 751.97 3.32 751.97 L 649.83 751.97 C 651.36 751.97 652.6 750.73 652.6 749.2 L 652.6 0.55 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.36 118.43)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:45.42em;--ltx-fo-height:45.22em;--ltx-fo-depth:7.95em;font-size:10pt;" height="735.68" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 625.67)" width="628.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:45.42em;">
<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Final Answer Synthesis Prompt<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000B3;">Contextual Note</span><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:
A potential conflict (indicated by </span><math id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) between internal parameter knowledge (</span><math id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) and external information (</span><math id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) might have been detected, with rationale </span><math id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#005959;">Your Task is to Synthesize the Best Final Answer (<math id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#005959;" mathcolor="#005959">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span>
<span id="A3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.8em;">
<span id="A3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Based on all inputs, identify the </span><span id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">best-supported single candidate answer</span><span id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Consider information recency, source reliability, and overall coherence, especially if a conflict (</span><math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c}=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) was detected.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="A3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If conflict (<math id="A3.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c}=1</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A3.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Explicitly address the discrepancy from </span><math id="A3.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I3.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Attempt to resolve it by selecting more credible information or state remaining uncertainty.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<span id="A3.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If no conflict (<math id="A3.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c}=0</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A3.I3.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Primarily ground your answer in </span><math id="A3.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I3.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, using </span><math id="A3.I3.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I3.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> as confirmation.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I3.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<span id="A3.I3.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I3.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Provide </span><span id="A3.I3.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">concise reasoning</span><span id="A3.I3.i5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for your chosen answer, citing relevant inputs (</span><math id="A3.I3.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p},\mathcal{E}_{c},r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p},\mathcal{E}_{c},r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I3.i5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">). Clearly state any remaining ambiguity or temporal uncertainty.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC6600;">Inputs Provided</span><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span>
<span id="A3.I4" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.8em;">
<span id="A3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question (<math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A3.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: {question}</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">parameter Knowledge Response (Consolidated <math id="A3.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A3.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: {consolidated_parameter_response}</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Context-derived Response (<math id="A3.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A3.I4.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: {context_aware_evidence_summary}</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Conflict Detection Flag (<math id="A3.I4.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A3.I4.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: {</span><math id="A3.I4.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I4.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">}</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I4.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Conflict Rationale (<math id="A3.I4.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A3.I4.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: {</span><math id="A3.I4.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I4.i5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">}</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;">Required Output Format for Final Answer (<math id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A3.SS4.p2.pic1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span>
<span id="A3.I5" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.8em;">
<span id="A3.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Final Answer</span><span id="A3.I5.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: …</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Reasoning for Final Answer</span><span id="A3.I5.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: … (Address conflict per </span><math id="A3.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I5.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> if </span><math id="A3.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c}=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I5.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Ambiguity/Uncertainty Assessment</span><span id="A3.I5.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: … (If any)</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Detailed Process Walkthrough</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We illustrate the complete CARE-RAG workflow using the NBA scoring example, as discussed in Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> (Stage I-IV visual overview) and referenced in the main text.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.5em;">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input Question (<math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>)</span>:
<span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"Who scored the most points in their NBA career?"</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">parameter Record Comparison (generates <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span>:
The LLM <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, using prompt <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\text{init}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>init</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\text{init}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Appendix <a href="#A3.SS1" title='C.1 Parameter Record Comparison Prompts (Π_"init" and Π_"iter") ‣ Appendix C Core Conflict-Aware and Reliable Evidence for RAG Prompts ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>), generates its initial context-free response <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. For this example, we assume <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math>, so the consolidated parameter-aware evidences <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> is: <span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"LeBron James"</span> (assuming the LLM’s parameter knowledge is up-to-date).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Retrieval Result Refinement (generates <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span>:
The retriever <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> returns evidences <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, e.g.:
<math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>: <span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"Kareem Abdul-Jabbar is the all-time leading scorer in the NBA, with 38,387 total points."</span>;
<math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>: <span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"Kareem rewriting scoring records."</span>;
<math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>: <span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"As of 2023, James holds the record."</span>

<br class="ltx_break">Using prompt <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Appendix <a href="#A3.SS2" title='C.2 Retrieval Result Refinement Prompt (Π_"ref") ‣ Appendix C Core Conflict-Aware and Reliable Evidence for RAG Prompts ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>), <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> processes <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> into the Context-aware evidence <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>. For example, <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> might be distilled to: <span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"Retrieved evidences state Kareem Abdul-Jabbar was the all-time leading scorer (38,387 points). One passage indicates that as of 2023, James holds the record, suggesting a change."</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conflict-Driven Summarization (generates <math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c},r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c},r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span>:
The conflict detector <math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, using prompt <math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> (Appendix <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Conflict Detection Prompt (Π_𝑐) ‣ Appendix C Core Conflict-Aware and Reliable Evidence for RAG Prompts ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>), compares <math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"LeBron James"</span>) with <math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"Retrieved evidences state Kareem… James holds the record…"</span>).

<br class="ltx_break">Assuming for clearer conflict demonstration that <math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> was distilled to only reflect outdated info like: <span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"According to retrieved text, Kareem Abdul-Jabbar is the top scorer."</span>

<br class="ltx_break">The outputs are:
Conflict Flag (<math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>): <math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Conflict Rationale (<math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>): <span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"parameter knowledge (<math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>) states LeBron James, while context-derived information (<math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>) states Kareem Abdul-Jabbar. These conflict."</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CARE-RAG Generation (generates <math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span>:
The LLM <math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, using prompt <math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\text{synth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>synth</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\text{synth}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Appendix <a href="#A3.SS4" title='C.4 CARE-RAG Generation Prompt (Π_"synth") ‣ Appendix C Core Conflict-Aware and Reliable Evidence for RAG Prompts ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>), receives <math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The <span id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Final Answer (<math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span> is, for example: <span id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"LeBron James is NBA’s all-time leading scorer. While some historical records mention Kareem Abdul-Jabbar, LeBron James has surpassed this record, aligning with current information."</span>

<br class="ltx_break">The <span id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reasoning</span> would acknowledge the conflict identified by <math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and explain the prioritization of current parameter knowledge (<math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>) or the more recent parts of <math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, treating Kareem’s record as historical.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Component Output Examples</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides additional, isolated examples of outputs from key components and stages of the Conflict-Aware and Reliable Evidence for RAG (CARE-RAG) framework. These examples illustrate the specific outputs for Context-aware evidence Generation (formerly Structured Reasoning), Conflict Detection, and CARE-RAG Generation. Examples for QA Repair (Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B QA Repair Module ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>) and parameter-aware evidence Generation (<math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, detailed in Appendix <a href="#A3.SS1" title='C.1 Parameter Record Comparison Prompts (Π_"init" and Π_"iter") ‣ Appendix C Core Conflict-Aware and Reliable Evidence for RAG Prompts ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>) are covered elsewhere or are straightforward.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="462.75" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 462.75" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,462.75) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FF4040;" fill="#FF4040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 459.3 C 0 461.21 1.55 462.75 3.46 462.75 L 649.69 462.75 C 651.6 462.75 653.15 461.21 653.15 459.3 L 653.15 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F2;" fill="#FFF2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 0.69 L 0.69 439.66 L 652.46 439.66 L 652.46 0.69 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.5 447.75)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.48em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="546.29"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.48em;">
<span id="A5.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">E.1 ★ Conflict Detection Output Example (<math id="A5.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c},r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">c</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c},r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A5.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">ℳ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.5 92.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:45.4em;--ltx-fo-height:24.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:6.09em;font-size:10pt;" height="423.23" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 338.9)" width="628.21"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A5.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:45.4em;">
<span id="A5.p2.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p2.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;">Task</span><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Evaluate whether the consolidated parameter-aware evidences (</span><math id="A5.p2.pic1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) contradict the refined Context-aware evidence (</span><math id="A5.p2.pic1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) for the given query. Output a conflict flag (</span><math id="A5.p2.pic1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) and a rationale (</span><math id="A5.p2.pic1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">). This uses prompt </span><math id="A5.p2.pic1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{c}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (Appendix </span><a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Conflict Detection Prompt (Π_𝑐) ‣ Appendix C Core Conflict-Aware and Reliable Evidence for RAG Prompts ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">).</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p2.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p2.pic1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;">Query (<math id="A5.p2.pic1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;" mathcolor="#E67E22">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:  </span><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Who was "Suite: Judy Blue Eyes" written about?</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p2.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p2.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;">Input: Consolidated parameter-aware evidences (<math id="A5.p2.pic1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#E67E22">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;" mathcolor="#E67E22">p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>) (simulated)</span><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span>
<span id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<span id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Stephen Stills wrote it about Judy Collins, his former girlfriend.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p2.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p2.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;">Input: Refined Context-aware evidence (<math id="A5.p2.pic1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#E67E22">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;" mathcolor="#E67E22">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>) (simulated)</span><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span>
<span id="A5.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<span id="A5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The song "Suite: Judy Blue Eyes" was written by Stephen Stills. It references Judy Collins and their relationship.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p2.pic1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p2.pic1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#9B59B6;">LLM Reasoning for Conflict Detection (part of <math id="A5.p2.pic1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9B59B6;" mathcolor="#9B59B6">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9B59B6;" mathcolor="#9B59B6">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span>
<span id="A5.I3" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<span id="A5.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Both inputs identify Stephen Stills as the author and Judy Collins as the subject.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The information provided is consistent and complementary, with no factual contradictions.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p2.pic1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p2.pic1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#E74C3C;">Conflict Detection Output</span><span id="A5.p2.pic1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span>
<span id="A5.I4" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<span id="A5.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Conflict Flag (<math id="A5.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A5.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:  </span><span id="A5.I4.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">0</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Conflict Rationale (<math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A5.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:  </span><span id="A5.I4.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">No conflict detected. Both parameter knowledge and context-derived information consistently identify Stephen Stills as the author and Judy Collins as the subject of the song.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="570.54" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 570.54" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,570.54) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#0000B3;" fill="#0000B3" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 567.22 C 0 569.05 1.49 570.54 3.32 570.54 L 649.83 570.54 C 651.66 570.54 653.15 569.05 653.15 567.22 L 653.15 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2FF;" fill="#F2F2FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.55 0.55 L 0.55 547.72 L 652.6 547.72 L 652.6 0.55 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.36 555.67)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="546.57"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.5em;">
<span id="A5.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">E.2 ✌ Context-aware evidence Generation Example (<math id="A5.p3.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A5.p3.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.36 268.79)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:45.42em;--ltx-fo-height:19.59em;--ltx-fo-depth:18.82em;font-size:10pt;" height="531.42" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 271.05)" width="628.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A5.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:45.42em;">
<span id="A5.p3.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p3.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;">Task</span><span id="A5.p3.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Distill the retrieved context (</span><math id="A5.p3.pic1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.p3.pic1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) into a concise and salient Context-aware evidence (</span><math id="A5.p3.pic1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.p3.pic1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">). This uses prompt </span><math id="A5.p3.pic1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.p3.pic1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (Appendix </span><a href="#A3.SS2" title='C.2 Retrieval Result Refinement Prompt (Π_"ref") ‣ Appendix C Core Conflict-Aware and Reliable Evidence for RAG Prompts ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization' class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a><span id="A5.p3.pic1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">).</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p3.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p3.pic1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.pic1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;">Input Question (<math id="A5.p3.pic1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;" mathcolor="#E67E22">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A5.p3.pic1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: </span><span id="A5.p3.pic1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Who was Henry Feilden?</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p3.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p3.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;">Input Retrieved Context (<math id="A5.p3.pic1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;" mathcolor="#E67E22">C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A5.p3.pic1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span>
<span id="A5.I5" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<span id="A5.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"Colonel Henry Wemyss Feilden CB (1838–1921) was a British Army officer, naturalist and Arctic explorer."</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"Feilden was the second son of the second Baronet Feilden…"</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"Henry Master Feilden (1818–1875) was a Conservative politician…"</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I5.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"Some sources incorrectly identify Henry Feilden as an actor."</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p3.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p3.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#9B59B6;">Generated Context-aware evidence (<math id="A5.p3.pic1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9B59B6;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#9B59B6">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9B59B6;" mathcolor="#9B59B6">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A5.p3.pic1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span>
<span id="A5.I6" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<span id="A5.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Key Factual Claims</span><span id="A5.I6.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span>
<span id="A5.I6.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1em;">
<span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Two distinct individuals named Henry Feilden are mentioned:</span></span>
<span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1em;">
<span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">*</span> 
<span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Colonel Henry Wemyss Feilden (1838–1921): British Army officer, naturalist, Arctic explorer.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">*</span> 
<span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Henry Master Feilden (1818–1875): Conservative politician.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I6.i1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The claim that a Henry Feilden was an actor is explicitly refuted for at least one, and implicitly for both if the context is considered complete regarding their professions.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Identified Ambiguities/Issues</span><span id="A5.I6.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: The query "Who was Henry Feilden?" is ambiguous without further specification, as the context provides two distinct individuals.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I6.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Context-Grounded Conclusion/Summary</span><span id="A5.I6.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: The retrieved context describes two notable individuals named Henry Feilden. To provide a specific answer to "Who was Henry Feilden?", clarification on which individual is being referred to would be necessary. The claim about Henry Feilden being an actor is noted as incorrect based on the context.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="512.69" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 512.69" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,512.69) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#009900;" fill="#009900" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 509.37 C 0 511.2 1.49 512.69 3.32 512.69 L 649.83 512.69 C 651.66 512.69 653.15 511.2 653.15 509.37 L 653.15 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2FFF2;" fill="#F2FFF2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.55 0.55 L 0.55 489.37 L 652.6 489.37 L 652.6 0.55 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.36 497.82)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.34" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="546.57"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.5em;">
<span id="A5.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">E.3 ▲ CARE-RAG Generation Output Example (<math id="A5.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A5.p4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\text{synth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">synth</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\text{synth}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.36 148.18)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:45.42em;--ltx-fo-height:24.09em;--ltx-fo-depth:10.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="473.08" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 333.32)" width="628.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A5.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:45.42em;">
<span id="A5.p4.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p4.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;">Task</span><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Generate the final reconciled answer (</span><math id="A5.p4.pic1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) by integrating all available information. This uses prompt </span><math id="A5.p4.pic1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\text{synth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">synth</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\text{synth}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (Appendix </span><a href="#A3.SS4" title='C.4 CARE-RAG Generation Prompt (Π_"synth") ‣ Appendix C Core Conflict-Aware and Reliable Evidence for RAG Prompts ‣ Rethinking All Evidence: Enhancing Trustworthy Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Conflict-Driven Summarization' class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">).</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p4.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p4.pic1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;">Input Question (<math id="A5.p4.pic1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;" mathcolor="#E67E22">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:  Who is the original artist of </span><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Sound of Silence</span><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, released in 1964?</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p4.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p4.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;">Input: Consolidated parameter-aware evidences (<math id="A5.p4.pic1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#E67E22">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;" mathcolor="#E67E22">p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>) (simulated)</span><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: </span><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Simon &amp; Garfunkel</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p4.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p4.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;">Input: Refined Context-aware evidence (<math id="A5.p4.pic1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#E67E22">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;" mathcolor="#E67E22">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>) (simulated)</span><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: </span><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Based on the provided context, Simon &amp; Garfunkel are identified as the original artists of "Sound of Silence" released in 1964. No conflicting information found in context.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p4.pic1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p4.pic1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;">Input: Conflict Flag (<math id="A5.p4.pic1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;" mathcolor="#E67E22">δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;" mathcolor="#E67E22">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: </span><math id="A5.p4.pic1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;">Input: Conflict Rationale (<math id="A5.p4.pic1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;" mathcolor="#E67E22">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#E67E22;" mathcolor="#E67E22">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p5.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: </span><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p5.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">No conflict detected between parameter knowledge and context-derived information.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p4.pic1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p4.pic1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#9B59B6;">CARE-RAG Generation Output (<math id="A5.p4.pic1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9B59B6;" mathcolor="#9B59B6">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span><span id="A5.p4.pic1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span>
<span id="A5.I7" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<span id="A5.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I7.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Final Answer</span><span id="A5.I7.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Simon &amp; Garfunkel were the original artists of the song "Sound of Silence," released in 1964.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I7.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Reasoning for Final Answer</span><span id="A5.I7.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Both the consolidated parameter knowledge (</span><math id="A5.I7.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I7.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) and the refined context-aware evidence (</span><math id="A5.I7.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℰ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I7.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) consistently identify Simon &amp; Garfunkel. The conflict flag (</span><math id="A5.I7.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c}=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I7.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) confirms no discrepancy was found. There is no ambiguity regarding the 1964 release.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I7.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Ambiguity/Uncertainty Assessment</span><span id="A5.I7.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: None detected.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
